1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
Graham told me to stop running his brother's workshop, so I stopped.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,580
Nine days later, inspectors shut the whole place down.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,800
I'm 31, a licensed structural engineer, married to Graham for four years.

4
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,480
His younger brother Reese opened the custom furniture shop four years ago

5
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:12,500
with a small business loan and no safety training at all.

6
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,540
From the very first month, I signed off on everything myself.

7
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,080
Shelving loads, mezzanine weight limits, wiring near the finishing booth.

8
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:18,280
Nobody paid me for it.

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:19,360
Nobody ever asked me to stop.

10
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:23,040
Then three weeks ago, a client watched me correct one of Reese's rigging diagrams in front of him,

11
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,700
and Reese told Graham I made him look incompetent in his own shop.

12
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,700
That night, Graham said I needed to let his brother run his own business for once.

13
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,900
I didn't argue. I just stopped answering Reese's text.

14
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:34,340
The annual recertification was due that same month, and I let the deadline pass without filing it.

15
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:37,980
Nine days later, the county fire marshal did a routine walkthrough and found no current structural

16
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:41,720
sign-off on file anywhere. He shut the shop down on the spot, pending a full recertification.

17
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,760
What Reese never knew was how close that shop had already come to disaster.

18
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:48,780
Two years ago, I found a mezzanine storage loft rated to hold half of what he was stacking on it.

19
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,280
Last spring, I caught wiring running six inches from the lacquer booth,

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:52,720
close enough to start a fire in seconds.

21
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:55,300
I fixed both quietly and told nobody, not even Graham.

22
00:00:55,300 --> 00:01:00,100
Reese had a delivery due for a hotel chain called Bellamy & Finch worth $82,000 due the second week

23
00:01:00,100 --> 00:01:03,640
of December, with a penalty clause for every day it was late. Closing the shop was costing

24
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:07,840
him roughly $1,000 a day. He called me 11 times in four days. I didn't answer once.

25
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:11,240
On the fifth day, I drove over to return a mixer I'd borrowed, not to check on him.

26
00:01:11,580 --> 00:01:13,800
Sitting open on his desk was the county's recertification binder.

27
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:17,460
A new structural sign-off page was already filed inside it, dated two days after our fight,

28
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:19,560
carrying my license number and a signature that was not mine.

29
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:23,060
I called the inspector's office listed on the form. She confirmed it had been accepted and

30
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:26,340
to reopen that same morning. I asked Graham if he'd known. He said,

31
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,840
Reese wouldn't do that. He did, I said. Graham stared at the binder, then asked,

32
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,620
You've been signing off on that place since the beginning?

33
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,640
Yes, I said. Why would he forge it instead of just calling you?

34
00:01:34,860 --> 00:01:38,820
Because he knew I'd say no. A forged engineering stamp is not a family disagreement.

35
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:41,820
It is a felony filed under my license number, not his.

36
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:45,660
I called the county that afternoon and reported the signature myself, before an inspector or

37
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:48,360
an insurance auditor found at first. The shop closed again within the hour,

38
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:52,140
this time flagged for fraud instead of a routine violation. Reese has not called since that day.

39
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:54,280
Graham sleeps on his own side of the bed again, not the couch,

40
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:55,940
but he has not brought up the workshop since either.

